{"id":"chatcmpl-969ba76a-3455-41de-8abd-b0387c351409","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229774,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When multiple perception tools return negative or conflicting results on a subtle finding, escalate to coordinate-based grounding to localize the abnormality and resolve laterality. Treat negative VQA outputs as potentially false negatives when the answer options imply a finding exists, and use spatial evidence plus explicit verification to arbitrate. The key is triangulating across complementary tools rather than trusting any single model's verdict.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When answer options presuppose a finding exists but initial detectors report 'none', treat the negatives as possible false negatives and escalate to a localization-capable tool.\",\n    \"Use coordinate-based grounding to convert ambiguous laterality questions into spatial evidence (image-left vs patient-right), then map coordinates to the correct option.\",\n    \"When tools conflict, insert an explicit verification step that states the proposed answer and the specific risk/conflict before finalizing.\",\n    \"Chain complementary perception methods (classification, grounded reporting, phrase grounding) so each compensates for the others' blind spots on subtle findings.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Prefer coordinate-grounded localization for laterality and subtle findings; don't accept a single model's 'absent' verdict when options imply presence.\",\n    \"Conflicting tool outputs\": \"Escalate to a more spatially precise tool, then run an explicit verify step naming the conflict and the risk of the tentative answer.\",\n    \"Subtle-finding detection\": \"Look for low-contrast signs (blunting, opacity) at expected anatomic landmarks and confirm against option wording before answering.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the localized coordinate maps to the correct patient side (image-left = patient-right) before selecting a laterality option.\",\n    \"Before finalizing, explicitly reconcile any negative detector outputs against the positive grounding evidence and state why the finding is real.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":658,"total_tokens":1043,"completion_tokens":385,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":658},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":385}}}